<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss March producer/import prices up 0.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Swiss March producer/import prices up 0.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The combined index for Swiss producer and import prices rose 0.2 percent in March for a year-on-year decline of 0.8 percent, the Federal Statistics Office said.  </p>
<p>The office released following details:</p>
<p>				  March 1997   Feb 1997   March 1996</p>
<p>Monthly pct index change  +0.2	   +0.2	 -0.2</p>
<p>Yr/yr pct index change    -0.8	   -1.2	 -2.3</p>
<p>Index (100 = May 1993)    97.0	   96.8	 97.9</p>
<p>Note - The combined producer/import price index replaced the wholesale price index in May 1993.  </p>
<p>The office also detailed the producer price index:</p>
<p>				  March 1997   Feb 1997   March 1996</p>
<p> Monthly pct index change +0.2	   -0.1	 -0.2</p>
<p> Yr/yr pct index change   -1.1	   -1.5	 -1.7</p>
<p> Index (100 = May 1993)   97.0	   96.8	 98.0</p>
<p>Import price index:</p>
<p>				  March 1997   Feb 1997   March 1996</p>
<p> Monthly pct index change +0.3	   +1.0	 0.0</p>
<p> Yr/yr pct index change   -0.3	   -0.6	 -3.6</p>
<p> Index (100 = May 1993)   97.2	   96.9	 97.5</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
